{"nodes": [{"id": "vault_system_how_it_works", "label": "GLUE: how it works now (SYSTEM.md)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "vault_system_glue_folder", "label": "GLUE folder (JSON store)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The user's data is JSON files in the GLUE folder, with no database. Lowercase mco names are the real file and setting names and stay, because existing data depends on them."}, {"id": "vault_system_local_link", "label": "Local link to GLUE Home (127.0.0.1)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ports 47400-47409 on 127.0.0.1. Any browser on the computer takes its link from GLUE Home. Every route except hello and connect needs the token; stopped, it answers only GLUE Home's own windows."}, {"id": "vault_system_rust_engine", "label": "GLUE Home's engine in Rust", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "GLUE Home is Rust since 0.59: its engine does the library's work, the analysis queue, the shared sync, the DJ libraries and its service, with one store per collection written straight to disk."}, {"id": "vault_system_no_writes_into_engine_dj", "label": "No writes into Engine DJ (0.80)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "After Engine DJ 5.3 rebuilt its Collection and the sync deleted the user's playlists, the sync is off unless engineWrites is set. Reading and following Engine DJ's libraries stay on."}, {"id": "vault_system_glue_home_engine_dj_library", "label": "GLUE Home's Engine DJ library of its own, shown as a drive", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Built as Engine DJ's Collection is and shown to Engine DJ as drive Z: (subst, Windows). Engine DJ 5.3 merges it with the Collection at each start. Only the top GLUE folder is GLUE's; written only while Engine DJ is closed, after a backup."}, {"id": "vault_system_rekordbox_xml_for_engine_dj", "label": "GLUE Home's rekordbox XML for Engine DJ", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The lists marked Keep in Engine DJ, as a rekordbox XML kept on this computer and not in the GLUE folder, because its paths are this computer's. Engine DJ reads it as its rekordbox library."}, {"id": "vault_system_main_dj_library", "label": "Main DJ library (one per computer)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Its grid and cues are a song's by default after GLUE's own; a song's BPM is GLUE's correction, then the main library's grid, then the analysis."}, {"id": "vault_system_engine_dj_kept_in_step_paused", "label": "Engine DJ kept in step both ways (phases 1 to 3, now paused)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Cues, loops and grids merged three ways per slot, then playlists kept in step, then playlists stayed in the DJ collection and edits from GLUE's collection went in. Paused by ADR 0194, which keeps the reading."}, {"id": "vault_system_collection_and_drive_copies", "label": "Engine DJ's Collection and its drives' copies", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Engine DJ shows the computer's Collection as the master; every playlist change is written there with one free id, then made in each drive's copy. The folder repair was turned off after it locked every playlist."}, {"id": "vault_system_shared_collection_sync", "label": "Shared collection sync through GLUE Cloud", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "GLUE Cloud keeps a snapshot and a log of changes; only changed files are looked at; a computer's own parts are written only by its own GLUE folder; clashes wait in a box and a computer never clashes with itself."}, {"id": "vault_system_songs_with_no_file", "label": "Songs with no file, matched and linked", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A DJ library's record whose file is gone is matched to the library's song with a certainty, and linked in bulk so its playlists and settings carry over and a new read keeps it linked."}, {"id": "vault_system_away_music_folders", "label": "Music folders that are away", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A network folder that is not connected is away, not gone: its songs are not marked missing, analysed, rescanned or written into, and they wait for it."}, {"id": "vault_system_gluey_tours", "label": "Gluey tours and help", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Tours are data pointing at data-guide parts of the UI; the first tour shows once per person, with seen kept across the browser, the GLUE folder and the account."}, {"id": "vault_system_native_analysis", "label": "Native audio analysis in GLUE Home", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The same analysis in Rust as a line-for-line port with JavaScript's numbers, held to the website's results; DSD is analysed as its 88.2 kHz PCM conversion, with a finding that says so."}], "edges": [{"source": "vault_system_how_it_works", "target": "vault_system_glue_folder", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "vault_system_how_it_works", "target": "vault_system_local_link", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "vault_system_how_it_works", "target": "vault_system_rust_engine", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "vault_system_how_it_works", "target": "vault_system_no_writes_into_engine_dj", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "vault_system_how_it_works", "target": "vault_system_glue_home_engine_dj_library", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "vault_system_how_it_works", "target": "vault_system_reko